opencv dnn: find the bundled flatbuffers headers first.

The TFLite importer's generated schema header asserts the exact version of
the flatbuffers headers OpenCV bundles. With the flatbuffers port staged,
its (newer) headers were found first and the build stopped on
"Non-compatible flatbuffers version included": OpenCV adds the bundled
directory as a system include directory, and the prefix's include directory
is one too and comes first. The bundled directory is now a plain -I, which
is searched before every system directory (naming it a second time with -I
does nothing: the compiler ignores -I for a directory it has as -isystem).

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/cmake/OpenCVDetectFlatbuffers.cmake
+++ b/cmake/OpenCVDetectFlatbuffers.cmake
@@ -3,6 +3,9 @@
   set(flatbuffers_VERSION "23.5.9")
   ocv_install_3rdparty_licenses(flatbuffers "${OpenCV_SOURCE_DIR}/3rdparty/flatbuffers/LICENSE.txt")
   ocv_add_external_target(flatbuffers "${OpenCV_SOURCE_DIR}/3rdparty/flatbuffers/include" "" "HAVE_FLATBUFFERS=1")
+  # Not a system directory: it has to be searched before the install prefix,
+  # where another flatbuffers may be (the generated schema asserts the version).
+  set_target_properties(ocv.3rdparty.flatbuffers PROPERTIES INTERFACE_SYSTEM_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES "")
   set(CUSTOM_STATUS_flatbuffers "    Flatbuffers:" "builtin/3rdparty (${flatbuffers_VERSION})")
 endif()
 
